:: Conclusion 1 {"position":"600,4900","size":"100,100"}
''Breaking News:'' It appears there was an attempted theft at a recent art exhibition, closed to the public. Hundreds of priceless pieces of art were on display, each with valuations of millions of dollars or more. However, a retired private investigator, Bruce, happened to be on the scene alongside his daughter, an artist who was invited. 

Details are scant but one suspect has been apprehended, and identified as a career art thief, “Joe M.” A second suspect was caught on camera entering in a large and unfashionable trench coat, but departed the scene prior to the attempted robbery and is believed to be responsible for an anonymous tip-off call to the authorities, immediately prior to the attempted theft.

Authorities have also found incendiary devices scattered around the premises, which they believe were intended to cover the theives’ escape by burning the remaining artwork. However, none of the incendiary devices were actually triggered.

[[End Game]]


