:: “I’ve actually been thinking about this, since we last spoke.” {"position":"3300,3800","size":"100,100"}
“I see the value in art as a medium of exchange for ideas. But I’ve also come to see it as an expression of our humanity, a record and an exploration of the absurd beauty of the human experience. But I also think it’s personal, and that everybody should find their own meaning in it.”

“That’s... verbose but also insightful. I always saw art as useless, a hobby for people with too much time, and something with no real utility or purpose.”

“But now... I suppose in the end there is no such thing as inherent meaning in anything, it’s all just arbitrary anyways. And if that’s the case, why shouldn’t we spend our time trying to create things that are beautiful or tragic or moving. I think I’ve found a reason to value art after all.”

[[I’m glad.]]

